---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import Draft from '../../components/Draft.astro';
import { addressLine, entity } from '../../lib/entity';
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'Terms of service', description: 'The terms version.cam is provided under.' }}>
	<Draft />
	<p>
		version.cam is provided by {entity.name}, {addressLine}, registration number {entity.registrationNumber} ("we"). These terms apply to
		anyone who uses the hosted service at version.cam, app.version.cam, api.version.cam and clips.version.cam
		("you"). The versioncam package on npm is under its own licence, the Functional Source License, and these
		terms do not change it.
	</p>

	<h2>The service</h2>
	<p>
		The service stores the recordings your CI publishes with <code>versioncam publish</code>, renders them,
		serves them at addresses that play the latest version, tells you when a clip stops matching your app, and
		reports on your pull requests through the Versioncam GitHub App. It never records your app itself: your CI
		does, with your own credentials, which never reach us.
	</p>

	<h2>Your account</h2>
	<p>
		You sign in with GitHub. Who may see and manage a project follows from GitHub: the members of the account
		where the Versioncam App is installed. You are responsible for who has access to your GitHub accounts and to
		any project token you make.
	</p>

	<h2>Your content</h2>
	<p>
		The recordings, their screens and the files rendered from them are yours. You give us the right to store,
		render and show them as your project's settings say (public, unlisted or private) and for no other purpose.
		You confirm that you may record and publish what your recordings show; if they show personal data, you are
		its controller and we process it for you under the data processing terms, which are part of these terms.
	</p>

	<h2>What you may not do</h2>
	<p>
		Use the service for anything unlawful; publish recordings you have no right to; try to reach other
		customers' data; overload the service on purpose; or use it to host files that are not recordings of your
		own product.
	</p>

	<h2>Plans and payment</h2>
	<p>
		Paid plans are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, through Stripe; prices exclude VAT, which is added
		where it applies. A subscription renews until you cancel it; cancelling takes effect at the end of the paid
		period. We tell you at least 30 days before a price changes, and a change never applies to a period you have
		already paid for. Refunds follow the <a href="/legal/refunds/">refund policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>When a plan ends</h2>
	<p>
		Your clips keep playing where they are embedded. What a lapsed plan no longer covers is described on the
		<a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>: new recordings of private projects beyond the free one are not stored,
		and versions older than the free plan keeps are removed sixty days after the plan ended.
	</p>

	<h2>Deleting</h2>
	<p>
		Deleting a project in the dashboard removes its recordings, renders and history from the service within an
		hour. Copies may remain in our providers' backups for up to 30 days, after which they are gone too. You can
		download any version's files before you delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>Availability</h2>
	<p>
		We work to keep the service available and your data safe, but we do not promise it will never be
		interrupted, except where a separate agreement says so. Your recordings also remain in your own CI, so the
		service is never the only copy of your work.
	</p>

	<h2>Liability</h2>
	<p>
		The service is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or
		consequential losses, and our total liability is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the
		claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, or the rights a
		consumer has under the law of their country.
	</p>

	<h2>Ending the agreement</h2>
	<p>
		You may stop using the service and delete your projects at any time. We may suspend an account that breaks
		these terms, telling you why, and end it if the breach is not put right.
	</p>

	<h2>Law</h2>
	<p>
		These terms are governed by the law of Slovenia, and its courts decide disputes, except that a consumer may
		also rely on the law and the courts of their own country. We may change these terms with 30 days' notice by
		email; the version in force is always this page.
	</p>

	<p>Questions: {entity.contactEmail}.</p>
</StarlightPage>
